00:41:06,280 --> 00:41:07,480
Windmill.

547
00:41:09,060 --> 00:41:11,310
Who built it? Some king?

548
00:41:12,520 --> 00:41:14,290
Just the men who used to live here.

549
00:41:14,600 --> 00:41:17,070
They must have been great builders, stacking stones so high.

550
00:41:17,910 --> 00:41:20,700
Winterfell has towers three times that size.

551
00:41:21,040 --> 00:41:23,370
"I'm Jon Snow and I'm from Winterfell.

552
00:41:23,640 --> 00:41:25,040
My daddy was a fancy lord

553
00:41:25,040 --> 00:41:27,780
and I lived in a tower that touched the clouds."

554
00:41:28,600 --> 00:41:30,150
If you're impressed by a windmill,

555
00:41:30,150 --> 00:41:33,050
you'd be swooning if you saw the Great Keep at Winterfell.

556
00:41:33,460 --> 00:41:34,670
What's swooning?

557
00:41:35,350 --> 00:41:36,320
Fainting.

558
00:41:37,660 --> 00:41:39,430
What's fainting?

559
00:41:42,300 --> 00:41:44,560
When a girl sees blood and collapses.

560
00:41:44,560 --> 00:41:46,460
Why would a girl see blood and collapse?

561
00:41:46,460 --> 00:41:47,320
Well...

562
00:41:49,470 --> 00:41:51,300
not all girls are like you.

563
00:41:52,710 --> 00:41:54,660
Well, girls see more blood than boys.

564
00:41:55,850 --> 00:41:58,570
Or do you like girls who swoon, Jon Snow?

565
00:41:59,430 --> 00:42:00,960
Oh, a spider!

566
00:42:00,960 --> 00:42:02,790
Save me, Jon Snow.

567
00:42:03,610 --> 00:42:07,920
My dress is made of the purest silk from Tralalalaleeday.

568
00:42:08,410 --> 00:42:10,480
I'd like to see you in a silk dress.

569
00:42:12,880 --> 00:42:13,780
Would you?

570
00:42:17,740 --> 00:42:19,630
So I could tear it off you.

571
00:42:20,590 --> 00:42:23,100
Well, you rip my pretty silk dress,

572
00:42:23,500 --> 00:42:25,170
I'll blacken your eye.

573
00:42:32,550 --> 00:42:34,780
Maybe one day I'll take you to Winterfell.

574
00:42:36,780 --> 00:42:38,910
Or maybe one day I'll take you there.

575
00:42:39,360 --> 00:42:41,500
After we've taken our land back.

576
00:42:44,920 --> 00:42:45,850
Ygritte.

577
00:42:49,370 --> 00:42:50,720
You won't win.

578
00:42:53,240 --> 00:42:55,350
I know your people are brave, no one denies that.

579
00:42:55,350 --> 00:42:56,290
You know nothing--

580
00:42:56,300 --> 00:42:58,490
Six times in the last thousand years,

581
00:42:58,490 --> 00:43:00,690
a King-Beyond-the-Wall has attacked the kingdoms.

582
00:43:01,140 --> 00:43:04,370
- Six times they failed. - And how do you know that?

583
00:43:04,370 --> 00:43:06,340
Every boy in the North knows it.

584
00:43:06,340 --> 00:43:07,980
We grow up learning it.

585
00:43:08,190 --> 00:43:09,290
Where the battles were fought,

586
00:43:09,290 --> 00:43:10,890
the names of the heroes, who died where.

587
00:43:11,110 --> 00:43:13,210
Six times you've invaded

588
00:43:13,210 --> 00:43:15,930
and six times you've failed.

589
00:43:16,920 --> 00:43:18,440
The seventh will be the same.

590
00:43:18,440 --> 00:43:21,320
- Mance is different. - You don't have the discipline.

591
00:43:21,620 --> 00:43:24,760
You don't have the training. Your army is no army.

592
00:43:25,370 --> 00:43:26,480
You don't know how to fight together.

593
00:43:26,480 --> 00:43:28,250
- You don't know that. - I do.

594
00:43:29,600 --> 00:43:30,760
I know it.

595
00:43:31,150 --> 00:43:33,270
If you attack the Wall, you'll die.

596
00:43:33,270 --> 00:43:34,460
All of you.

597
00:43:43,630 --> 00:43:44,910
All of us.

598
00:44:01,440 --> 00:44:02,470
You're mine

599
00:44:03,470 --> 00:44:05,090
as I'm yours.

600
00:44:06,350 --> 00:44:08,260
And if we die, we die.

601
00:44:09,640 --> 00:44:11,490
But first we'll live.

602
00:44:12,210 --> 00:44:15,300
Yes, first we'll live.

603
00:44:32,460 --> 00:44:34,090
What's he going on about?

604
00:44:35,200 --> 00:44:37,410
And how come he always gets to sit and chat

605
00:44:37,790 --> 00:44:39,390
while we do all the work?

606
00:44:42,600 --> 00:44:43,460
Hodor.

607
00:44:46,190 --> 00:44:48,040
- That's where we are. - What are you telling him?

608
00:44:49,470 --> 00:44:51,060
- It's all right, Osha. - It's not all right.

609
00:44:51,060 --> 00:44:52,990
You think I can't hear you every day?

610
00:44:52,990 --> 00:44:54,840
Filling his head with black magic.

611
00:44:55,210 --> 00:44:57,930
Talking about visions and three-eyed ravens and worse.

612
00:44:57,930 --> 00:45:00,330
- Leave him alone. - He can speak for himself.

613
00:45:00,800 --> 00:45:02,230
I don't fill his head with anything.

614
00:45:02,700 --> 00:45:04,080
So what do you talk about?

615
00:45:05,360 --> 00:45:08,040
What's happening to him and what that means.

616
00:45:08,040 --> 00:45:10,810
Go on, then. Tell us what it means.

617
00:45:10,810 --> 00:45:12,060
It's not like that.

618
00:45:12,620 --> 00:45:14,140
I wish I could tell him all the answers.

619
00:45:14,140 --> 00:45:15,460
It would be much easier.

620
00:45:17,110 --> 00:45:18,990
I don't want you talking to him anymore.

621
00:45:18,990 --> 00:45:21,020
Until we get to your brother at Castle Black.

622
00:45:21,020 --> 00:45:22,980
- We're not going to Castle Black. - What did you say?

623
00:45:24,240 --> 00:45:27,140
I told you already. Jon Snow isn't there.

624
00:45:27,750 --> 00:45:29,620
Bran needs to find the raven beyond the Wall.

625
00:45:29,620 --> 00:45:30,880
Oh, no. I'm not going back there.

626
00:45:30,880 --> 00:45:33,820
Your brother is at Castle Black. That's where we're going.

627
00:45:35,920 --> 00:45:37,320
Look at me.

628
00:45:39,320 --> 00:45:42,610
The raven's been coming to me ever since I fell from that tower.

629
00:45:43,380 --> 00:45:45,120
He wants me to find him.

630
00:45:46,330 --> 00:45:48,530
I don't have my legs anymore.

631
00:45:49,930 --> 00:45:51,380
This is what I have now.

632
00:45:51,380 --> 00:45:53,270
You have a family.

633
00:45:53,730 --> 00:45:55,460
You need to go back to Castle Black

634
00:45:55,460 --> 00:45:58,240
so you can get back to them where you belong.

635
00:45:58,240 --> 00:45:59,830
What if I belong in the North?

636
00:46:01,150 --> 00:46:05,620
What if I fell from that tower for a reason?

637
00:46:06,260 --> 00:46:07,530
Is that what he's telling you?

638
00:46:07,990 --> 00:46:09,540
That it's all for a reason?

639
00:46:10,310 --> 00:46:11,180
All these bad things

640
00:46:11,180 --> 00:46:13,700
happened because the gods got big plans for you?

641
00:46:14,970 --> 00:46:16,440
I wish it were true, little lord.

642
00:46:16,440 --> 00:46:17,570
But the gods wouldn't spare

643
00:46:17,570 --> 00:46:20,620
a raven's cold shit for you or me or anyone.

644
00:46:20,620 --> 00:46:22,340
You don't understand. You don't know.

645
00:46:22,340 --> 00:46:24,690
You don't know. None of you know.

646
00:46:24,690 --> 00:46:26,250
None of you have been up there.

647
00:46:30,150 --> 00:46:31,610
I had a man once.

648
00:46:32,450 --> 00:46:33,570
A good man.

649
00:46:34,310 --> 00:46:35,740
Bruni, his name was.

650
00:46:36,120 --> 00:46:38,550
I was his and he was mine.

651
00:46:39,300 --> 00:46:41,170
But one night Bruni disappears.

652
00:46:42,480 --> 00:46:43,840
People said he left me,

653
00:46:44,790 --> 00:46:45,900
but I knew him.

654
00:46:46,340 --> 00:46:49,740
He'd never leave me. Not for long.

655
00:46:50,850 --> 00:46:52,280
I knew he'd come back.

656
00:46:54,260 --> 00:46:55,250
And he did.

657
00:46:57,480 --> 00:46:59,640
He came in through the back of the hut.

658
00:47:01,600 --> 00:47:03,210
Only it wasn't Bruni.

659
00:47:03,670 --> 00:47:04,680
Not really.

660
00:47:06,710 --> 00:47:11,720
His skin was pale like a dead man's.

661
00:47:13,260 --> 00:47:15,760
His eyes bluer than clear sky.

662
00:47:19,390 --> 00:47:20,660
He came at me,

663
00:47:21,270 --> 00:47:26,350
grabbed me by the neck and squeezed so hard

664
00:47:26,350 --> 00:47:28,980
I could feel the life slipping out of me.

665
00:47:31,770 --> 00:47:33,640
I don't know how I got the knife.

666
00:47:34,110 --> 00:47:39,270
When I did, I stuck it deep into his heart.

667
00:47:42,800 --> 00:47:45,100
And he hardly seemed to notice.

668
00:47:47,020 --> 00:47:50,720
I had to burn our hut down with him inside.

669
00:47:53,760 --> 00:47:55,850
I didn't ask the gods what it meant.

670
00:47:56,370 --> 00:47:58,890
I didn't need to. I already knew.

671
00:48:00,290 --> 00:48:02,860
It meant the North was no place for men to be.

672
00:48:03,540 --> 00:48:04,850
Not anymore.

673
00:48:07,740 --> 00:48:10,210
I promised your maester I'd get you to Castle Black

674
00:48:10,210 --> 00:48:11,720
and no further.

675
00:48:21,090 --> 00:48:23,060
How is the pain, my lord?

676
00:48:26,040 --> 00:48:28,760
What's the purpose of an arm with no hand?

677
00:48:33,040 --> 00:48:35,080
Well, we've stymied the corruption.

678
00:48:35,700 --> 00:48:37,980
Yes, we've stymied the corruption.

679
00:48:38,590 --> 00:48:39,980
You're a learned man.

680
00:48:40,720 --> 00:48:42,070
All the good it's done me.

681
00:48:42,070 --> 00:48:44,230
You did well sewing up this mess.

682
00:48:45,140 --> 00:48:48,890
You're far better at this sort of work than Grand Maester Pycelle.

683
00:48:49,690 --> 00:48:51,830
Faint praise, my lord.

684
00:48:53,870 --> 00:48:56,330
So why did the Citadel take your chain?

685
00:48:57,120 --> 00:48:59,020
Did you fondle one boy too many?

686
00:48:59,020 --> 00:49:01,600
No, my lord. That's not my weakness.

687
00:49:03,710 --> 00:49:04,750
What is?

688
00:49:08,280 --> 00:49:09,400
Curiosity.

689
00:49:09,840 --> 00:49:13,460
The only way to treat disease is to understand disease.

690
00:49:14,200 --> 00:49:15,870
And the only way to understand it

691
00:49:15,870 --> 00:49:17,720
is to study the afflicted.

692
00:49:18,900 --> 00:49:21,010
You performed experiments on living men.

693
00:49:21,010 --> 00:49:23,070
- On dying men. - With their permission?

694
00:49:23,070 --> 00:49:25,740
My studies have given me insight

695
00:49:26,650 --> 00:49:27,900
that has saved many lives.

696
00:49:27,900 --> 00:49:29,540
Dying paupers, I assume.

697
00:49:30,390 --> 00:49:32,710
Men with no families to complain.

698
00:49:34,050 --> 00:49:35,780
You found them moaning in the poorhouse

699
00:49:35,780 --> 00:49:37,650
and had them carted back to your garret

700
00:49:38,540 --> 00:49:41,480
and opened up their bellies to see what was inside.

701
00:49:41,480 --> 00:49:43,360
How many men have you killed, my lord?

702
00:49:44,940 --> 00:49:45,770
I don't know.

703
00:49:45,770 --> 00:49:48,570
50? 100?

704
00:49:50,650 --> 00:49:51,810
Countless.

705
00:49:52,950 --> 00:49:54,620
Countless has a nice ring to it.

706
00:49:54,620 --> 00:49:56,440
And how many lives have you saved?

707
00:49:57,300 --> 00:49:58,710
Half a million.

708
00:50:01,090 --> 00:50:03,050
The population of King's Landing.

709
00:50:08,490 --> 00:50:10,740
You were in charge of the ravens at Harrenhal.

710
00:50:11,960 --> 00:50:16,210
Did you-- did you get a bird off to Brienne's father in Tarth?

711
00:50:16,390 --> 00:50:18,660
A bird flew off and a bird flew back.

712
00:50:19,980 --> 00:50:21,880
Lord Selwyn Tarth

713
00:50:22,650 --> 00:50:26,100
offered 300 gold dragons for his daughter's safe return.

714
00:50:26,610 --> 00:50:30,010
- A fair offer. - A fair offer. Locke won't take it.

715
00:50:31,930 --> 00:50:33,060
Why not?

716
00:50:33,440 --> 00:50:34,860
He's convinced Lord Tarth

717
00:50:34,860 --> 00:50:37,460
owns all the sapphire mines in Westeros.

718
00:50:38,900 --> 00:50:40,530
He feels he's being cheated.

719
00:50:42,020 --> 00:50:43,470
They'd be fools to kill her.

720
00:50:43,870 --> 00:50:45,980
These men have been at war a long time.

721
00:50:45,980 --> 00:50:47,920
Most of them will be dead by winter.

722
00:50:48,450 --> 00:50:50,770
She'll be their entertainment tonight.

723
00:50:51,800 --> 00:50:53,120
Beyond tonight,

724
00:50:53,700 --> 00:50:55,360
I don't think they care very much.

725
00:51:15,040 --> 00:51:16,600
We have to return to Harrenhal.

726
00:51:18,040 --> 00:51:18,710
Why?

727
00:51:18,710 --> 00:51:20,200
I've left something behind.

728
00:51:20,200 --> 00:51:21,520
Absolutely not.

729
00:51:22,060 --> 00:51:23,890
I've got orders from Lord Bolton.

730
00:51:23,890 --> 00:51:25,620
And what are those orders?

731
00:51:25,620 --> 00:51:28,370
To deliver you to your father at King's Landing.

732
00:51:29,600 --> 00:51:31,490
You think you'll get a reward.

733
00:51:33,350 --> 00:51:35,960
I serve Lord Bolton.

734
00:51:36,480 --> 00:51:37,750
Any appreciation your father--

735
00:51:37,750 --> 00:51:39,170
You think you're getting a reward.

736
00:51:39,170 --> 00:51:40,690
Let me explain something to you.

737
00:51:40,850 --> 00:51:42,550
When my father sees me, the first thing

738
00:51:42,550 --> 00:51:44,600
he's going to ask is what happened to my hand.

739
00:51:44,960 --> 00:51:47,870
And I'm going to tell him this man chopped it off.

740
00:51:47,870 --> 00:51:51,980
- I had nothing-- - Or I could tell him this man saved my life.

741
00:51:53,970 --> 00:51:56,350
We return to Harrenhal now.

742
00:52:19,490 --> 00:52:21,150
- Eyes open, lads. - Be quiet.

743
00:52:26,800 --> 00:52:29,640
*The bear, the bear. The maiden fair.*

744
00:52:29,980 --> 00:52:32,260
*From there to here. From here to there!*

745
00:52:32,260 --> 00:52:33,470
*All black and brown, and covered with hair!*

746
00:52:33,470 --> 00:52:36,640
*He smelled the scent on the summer air.*

747
00:52:36,640 --> 00:52:40,600
*The bear, the bear. The maiden fair.*

748
00:52:44,080 --> 00:52:44,960
Don't spare her.

749
00:52:45,880 --> 00:52:47,150
Don't spare her!

750
00:52:50,160 --> 00:52:53,430
Well, this is one shameful fucking performance.

751
00:52:53,430 --> 00:52:55,190
Stop running and fight.

752
00:53:02,370 --> 00:53:04,020
A wooden sword?

753
00:53:04,200 --> 00:53:07,250
- I thought you'd gone. - You gave her a wooden sword.

754
00:53:07,370 --> 00:53:08,660
We've only got one bear.

755
00:53:08,660 --> 00:53:10,270
I'll pay her bloody ransom.

756
00:53:10,470 --> 00:53:12,430
Gold, sapphires, whatever you want.

757
00:53:12,430 --> 00:53:13,860
Just get her out of there.

758
00:53:14,100 --> 00:53:16,060
All you lords and ladies

759
00:53:16,670 --> 00:53:19,360
still think that the only thing that matters is gold.

760
00:53:20,070 --> 00:53:23,210
This makes me happier than all your gold ever could.

761
00:53:23,450 --> 00:53:25,910
And that makes me happier than all her sapphires.

762
00:53:25,910 --> 00:53:28,300
So go buy yourself a golden hand

763
00:53:28,300 --> 00:53:30,380
and fuck yourself with it.

764
00:53:49,930 --> 00:53:51,420
- Get behind me. - I will not.

765
00:54:02,730 --> 00:54:04,710
What the fuck are you doing to my bear?

766
00:54:04,710 --> 00:54:06,840
Lord Bolton charged me with bringing him back

767
00:54:06,840 --> 00:54:09,710
to King's Landing alive and that's what I aim to do.

768
00:54:13,310 --> 00:54:14,250
Pull her up.

769
00:54:28,370 --> 00:54:29,740
Hold my legs.

770
00:54:53,100 --> 00:54:54,300
Pull him up!

771
00:55:05,040 --> 00:55:06,730
The bitch stays.

772
00:55:09,930 --> 00:55:11,680
We're taking her to King's Landing.

773
00:55:12,070 --> 00:55:13,400
Unless you kill me.

774
00:55:15,990 --> 00:55:17,480
She belongs to me.

775
00:55:18,170 --> 00:55:20,100
Lord Bolton's orders.

776
00:55:20,580 --> 00:55:22,710
What do you think is more important to Lord Bolton?

777
00:55:23,690 --> 00:55:25,040
Getting his pet rat a reward

778
00:55:25,040 --> 00:55:27,950
or ensuring Tywin Lannister gets his son back alive?

779
00:55:49,040 --> 00:55:51,060
Well, we must be on our way.

780
00:55:55,510 --> 00:55:57,230
Sorry about the sapphires.

